<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Prediction Impact</title>
    <style>
        h3 { ${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE} }
        body { ${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE} }
        code { ${MONOSPACE_FONT_STYLE} }
        h3 code { font-size: inherit; }
        p { margin-top: 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h3>Prediction Impact</h3>
    <p>How much each column actually drove the predictions of <em>this</em> model, measured over the test rows.</p>
    <p>A column can matter for the data but not for the model. If two columns say almost the same thing, the model leans on one and the other drops to nothing here.</p>
    <p>Calculated from <code>PREDICTION_DETAILS</code>. Oracle AutoML computes its own Prediction Impact a different way, so the two are not directly comparable.</p>
</body>
</html>
